{"id": "EUVD-2026-28621", "enisaUuid": "eb9822c3-aa74-3a16-a56c-047fe66052e4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Fix NULL pointer dereference in dcn401_init_hw()\n\ndcn401_init_hw() assumes that update_bw_bounding_box() is valid when\nentering the update path. However, the existing condition:\n\n  ((!fams2_enable && update_bw_bounding_box) || freq_changed)\n\ndoes not guarantee this, as the freq_changed branch can evaluate to true\nindependently of the callback pointer.\n\nThis can result in calling update_bw_bounding_box() when it is NULL.\n\nFix this by separating the update condition from the pointer checks and\nensuring the callback, dc->clk_mgr, and bw_params are validated before\nuse.\n\nFixes the below:\n../dc/hwss/dcn401/dcn401_hwseq.c:367 dcn401_init_hw() error: we previously assumed 'dc->res_pool->funcs->update_bw_bounding_box' could be null (see line 362)\n\n(cherry picked from commit 86117c5ab42f21562fedb0a64bffea3ee5fcd477)", "datePublished": "2026-05-08T13:31:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:40:39", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fcc51c81cb472eb460310c477460356dc4845ff7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/10c13c111d0d7f8e101c742feff264fc98e3f9f7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2d4a6f0702c5211e0be8b688c5fc24f082ec74d6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e927b36ae18b66b49219eaa9f46edc7b4fdbb25e"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-43337", "GHSA-5cr7-8523-mgr2"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1c6935ef-c015-3175-a6eb-8e3e6b103a57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ca0fb243c3bb53dbbd71d16c76f319bf923ee3d4 <fcc51c81cb472eb460310c477460356dc4845ff7"}, {"id": "4178e2d8-c06d-351c-8d7f-0d184182229e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ca0fb243c3bb53dbbd71d16c76f319bf923ee3d4 <2d4a6f0702c5211e0be8b688c5fc24f082ec74d6"}, {"id": "51925ea2-71df-36a5-b1b3-f3dcf33a9f6f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "5e19be8e-cce9-3297-819d-e6a058afe1bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}, {"id": "6753ca9d-2e0b-3d96-8d93-6a0e021536b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "7ccc86f8-b360-34fc-bddd-645d600eb653", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ca0fb243c3bb53dbbd71d16c76f319bf923ee3d4 <e927b36ae18b66b49219eaa9f46edc7b4fdbb25e"}, {"id": "858b489e-1b8f-3590-9351-419293dfab43", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ca0fb243c3bb53dbbd71d16c76f319bf923ee3d4 <10c13c111d0d7f8e101c742feff264fc98e3f9f7"}, {"id": "98d71cc3-8614-3f6f-b01d-a7b7db038cbf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.12"}, {"id": "c5ed0211-9704-3209-b2a3-416393248034", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.22"}, {"id": "dd719bdc-770d-35d5-8864-ed79c5c3036b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11.3 <6.12"}, {"id": "e17c9adf-c153-368b-9744-f98e0b3e0a6f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e13689793b9c0e7b5749954e77f5f85e68fe7138"}, {"id": "ee95eace-1bb1-3bd5-827f-7201f9b7845b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "df92da8c-266a-3317-a62c-575ae7e22e02", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}